      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "Given that $f(x)=({x}^{2}+3)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x),$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,+$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)={x}^{2}+3$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x).$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={({x}^{2}+3)}^{′}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)+({x}^{2}+3){(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x))}^{′} \\\\  & =(2x)(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x))+({x}^{2}+3)(\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)+\\frac{{x}^{2}+3}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
